37. Security and separation of duties
The following controls are mandatory:

Finance Officers must not edit student academic results.

Lecturers must not access student financial transaction details by default.

Students must only access their own statements and invoices.

Payment confirmation must be server-side.

M-Pesa callbacks must be validated and idempotent.

Posted payments must not be deleted.

Refunds require authorization.

High-value transactions require additional approval.

Invoice adjustments must be auditable.

Financial exports must be permission-controlled.

General ledger posting must preserve debit-credit balance.

Supplier creation and supplier payment approval should be separated where possible.

Finance users must not approve their own restricted transactions.

Bank reconciliation changes must retain history.

Financial audit logs must be protected from modification.

38. Acceptance criteria
The Finance Portal is ready for production review only when:

Fee structures can be configured and versioned.

Invoices can be generated and tracked.

Student statements calculate correctly.

M-Pesa payment callbacks are validated.

Duplicate payment processing is prevented.

Payments can be allocated accurately.

Receipts can be generated and verified.

Bank statements can be reconciled.

Refunds follow approval workflows.

Scholarships and waivers are auditable.

Supplier invoices and payments are tracked.

Double-entry accounting is enforced.

Budget commitments and expenditure reconcile.

Financial reports use posted transaction data.

Student portal access is restricted to authorized records.

Financial approval limits are enforced by the backend.

Critical workflows have automated tests.

Backup and recovery procedures are verified.

